  "method": [
    "The seven shares are those of the companies on this dashboard. A share joins both indexes at the first month end for which the price source has a price: UL Solutions in April 2024, the month it listed, and TIC Solutions in February 2025. The other five are in from the start.",
    "Each month's return for a share is the change in its month-end closing price adjusted for dividends and splits, so dividends count as reinvested. Returns are in the share's own currency: Swiss francs, US dollars, euros, sterling or Australian dollars. No share price is converted.",
    "Equal-weighted index: each month's return is the plain average of the returns of the shares in the index. It is rebalanced to equal weights every month.",
    "Market-cap-weighted index: each month's return is the average weighted by market cap at the previous month end. Market caps are reset at each year end to the US dollar figures published by a market-data site, and in between they move month by month with each share's return.",
    "Both indexes are 100 at the end of December 2020 and run to the last complete month."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The indexes stop at the last complete month end, 30 October 2026. Share-price moves in November 2026 are not in them, including the fall of about 12% in ALS shares on 23 November reported under TIC earnings news.",
    "Prices come from market-data sites, not from the exchanges, and are rounded to two decimals. They carry the secondary_report label.",
    "The indexes mix currencies without converting them, so they show share performance in local terms. An investor in one currency would also have had the currency moves.",
    "Market caps are converted to US dollars by the site that publishes them. This is the one place on the dashboard where currencies are put on a common basis, and only to set weights.",
    "Between year ends a weight moves with the share's total return. It does not pick up currency moves, dividends paid out, buy-backs or new shares.",
    "TIC Solutions has a single market cap, for October 2026. Working back from it overstates the company's weight before the NV5 merger in August 2025, when it had fewer shares. It has the smallest weight throughout.",
    "The price source starts TIC Solutions in February 2025, when it was still named Acuren, so it joins the indexes then.",
    "UL Solutions month-end prices were read for November 2025 onwards. Earlier months use published monthly returns rounded to 0.1 point.",
    "These indexes are calculated for this dashboard. They are not published benchmarks and cannot be bought. This is not investment advice."
  ]
}
